# Consumption order for ewinregirgojr/MiniCPM5-1B-Agentic-Tooluse-Merged-FP16.
#
# A LlamaForCausalLM: 24 layers, hidden 1536, 16 heads of 128 over
# 2 KV heads, intermediate 4608, vocabulary 130,560, stored F16. Read
# from the Llama forward pass exactly as layouts/smollm2-135m.order
# reads it, per layer q, k, v, o, gate, up, down:
#
#   h = x + o_proj(attn(q_proj(rms(x)), k_proj(rms(x)), v_proj(rms(x))))
#   y = h + down_proj(silu(gate_proj(rms(h))) * up_proj(rms(h)))
#
# The names below are the checkpoint's own, from its safetensors
# headers (sha256 ad304762...a499a6 and 3f1dd81d...45322b in the
# Hugging Face cache); the order file was generated from that list
# and this forward pass, and spm-order refuses it if either disagrees
# with the other.
#
# UNTIED EMBEDDINGS, unlike SmolLM2. `lm_head.weight` is its own
# 200,540,160-weight matrix, applied in full to every token after the final
# norm -- so it is the last ROTATING stream, swept once per token. The
# input embedding is gathered by token id and stays [resident], as do
# the 49 RMS norm scales (75,264 weights).
#
# Rotating 880,017,408 of 1,080,632,832 weights (81.4%); resident
# 200,615,424 (18.6%), of which the embedding is 200,540,160.
#
# Why this model: it is the real checkpoint nearest to hand that a
# scheduler can be shaped by. sw-os-ml (M3 step 010) reads the sidecar
# `emufpga import --sidecar-only` writes from this order -- the tensor
# inventory and the rotating boundary, kilobytes of text -- to build a
# decode-loop access trace with a real model's shape rather than an
# invented one. The weights themselves are never imported here.

[rotating]
model.layers.0.self_attn.q_proj.weight
model.layers.0.self_attn.k_proj.weight
model.layers.0.self_attn.v_proj.weight
model.layers.0.self_attn.o_proj.weight
model.layers.0.mlp.gate_proj.weight
model.layers.0.mlp.up_proj.weight
model.layers.0.mlp.down_proj.weight
